# Skip Nix-darwin's /etc/zshrc: it runs an unconditional compinit +
# compaudit + promptinit, then Oh My Zsh runs compinit again. The duplicate
# compinit doubled startup time and caused intermittent 1.5-3s shells
# whenever .zcompdump went stale. OMZ sets its own history options, emacs
# keymap, and theme, so nothing from /etc/zshrc is needed.
NOSYSZSHRC=1
